deletedBillto.zip contains an almost standalone set of testdata. All it needs
is the standard AdNovum test materials.

There is a sold-to, ship-to and bill-to as well as a contract. Once imported,
you can locate them with 'Deleted Billto' (ship-to search).

In the original state of the test requests, both the sold-to and the bill-to
are valid bill-to's for the sold-to/ship-to pair. Verify that.

Then, in a second step, locate the line in soldto.request which is currently
commented out (<MSGFN>003</MSGFN>). Replace the 005 in the line below (which
is not commented out) by 003. That means that you are deleting the bill-to
partner function of the sold-to to itself. Thus, the sold-to cannot be his own
bill-to anymore.

After sending the data again (and without saving the dispocard after that),
verify that the sold-to is not available as bill-to in any of order taking,
dispocard or order details.
